#: ../../configuration.rst:232
msgid "Identification of users"
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:234
msgid ""
"Apple School Manager identifies a user by the ``person_id`` column. The "
"connector fills it with an LDAP attribute of the user that doesn't change"
" when you rename the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:240
#, python-format
msgid "LDAP attribute that identifies a teacher. Default: ``%entryUUID``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:245
#, python-format
msgid "LDAP attribute that identifies a student. Default: ``%entryUUID``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:250
msgid ""
"Don't change these variables on a running installation. Apple School "
"Manager treats a user with a new ``person_id`` as a different user and "
"loses the association with the existing account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:258
msgid "Password policy for students"
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:260
msgid ""
"Apple School Manager creates the password for a new student itself. The "
"password policy determines how long that password is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:265
msgid ""
"Length of the password that Apple creates for a new student. Valid values"
" are ``4``, ``6``, ``8``, and the dash (``-``). The dash means that Apple"
" School Manager uses the default of the school. Default: ``4``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:270
msgid ""
"Apple School Manager doesn't support a password policy for teachers. A "
"value other than the ones listed makes the synchronization stop with an "
"error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:277
msgid "Grade level of students"
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:281
msgid ""
"LDAP attribute that holds the grade level of a student. The connector "
"exports its value in the ``grade_level`` column. Default: unset, which "
"leaves the column empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:288
msgid "Names of courses and classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:290
msgid ""
"UCS\\@school prefixes the name of a school class with the school "
"abbreviation, for example ``gym123-1a``. The connector derives the course"
" name from that name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:296
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Pattern for the course name. The connector replaces ``{ou}`` with the "
"school abbreviation and ``{name}`` with the class name without the school"
" prefix. Default: ``{ou}-{name}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:303
msgid ""
"Leaves the ``class_number`` column empty. Apple School Manager builds the"
" name of a class from the course name and the class number, so an "
"identical class number only repeats the course name. Default: ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:312
msgid "Select users with an LDAP filter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:314
msgid ""
"If the school list from :ref:`configuration-school-list` isn't fine-"
"grained enough, you can select the users with an LDAP filter. The "
"connector applies the filter in addition to the school list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:321
msgid "LDAP filter for the students of every school."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:325
msgid "LDAP filter for the teachers of every school."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:327
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A filter for an individual school overrides the global filter. Append the"
" school abbreviation to the variable name for that, as in "
":samp:`asm/ldap_filter/students/{gym123}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:331
msgid "Synchronize only the students of one class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../configuration.rst:338
msgid ""
"An invalid LDAP filter stops the synchronization. The connector uploads "
"nothing in that case, so the data in Apple School Manager stays as it was"
" after the last successful run."
msgstr ""

